{
    "background_story": "Gabriela was a young opera singer with a voice that echoed the great Enrico Caruso. Growing up in a family of modest means, she was discovered by a local music teacher who recognized her incredible talent. With dedication and hard work, Gabriela honed her craft, studying the great Italian operas and perfecting her technique. Her big break came when she was cast as Mimi in La Boh\u00e8me, opposite a renowned tenor. Her performance was met with rave reviews, with critics praising her powerful, expressive voice and charismatic stage presence. Soon, Gabriela was in demand, performing on the world's most famous opera stages, from La Scala to the Met. Her voice, like Caruso's, was a gift from the gods, capable of conveying the deepest emotions and moving audiences to tears.",
